dynamical-law-1a062f12.conceptual_definition:
This formula, known as the Dynamical Law for Rotational Motion or Newton's Second Law for Rotation, states that the net external torque acting on a system is equal to the rate of change of the system's angular momentum. It is the rotational analog to Newton's second law (
\( \mathbf{F} = \frac{d\mathbf{p}}{dt} \)
) for linear motion.
